Subject: gstreamer: disconnect requestCompleted when the camera is closed

libcamerasrc connects the camera's requestCompleted signal on every open and
never disconnects it. When the camera manager outlives the session (in neo-camera
it did on some switches: 4 opens, 3 managers), opening that camera again
delivers each request twice: a use-after-free in readMetadata() or a wrong
pop of queuedRequests_. neo-camera crashed on front/back switches (S10e).

--- a/src/gstreamer/gstlibcamerasrc.cpp	2026-11-12 06:21:11.254791416 +0100
+++ b/src/gstreamer/gstlibcamerasrc.cpp	2026-11-12 06:21:11.282581477 +0100
@@ -962,6 +962,16 @@
 
 	state->config_.reset();
 
+	/*
+	 * Undo the connect() of gst_libcamera_src_open(). The camera manager can
+	 * outlive this session (a device monitor, or another element, holds it),
+	 * and with it the camera: opened again, it would deliver every request
+	 * to this handler once per earlier session. The second delivery reads a
+	 * request the first one already freed, or pops the next queued request
+	 * ("wrap->request_.get() == request" fails) and frees it under libcamera.
+	 */
+	state->cam_->requestCompleted.disconnect(state, &GstLibcameraSrcState::requestCompleted);
+
 	ret = state->cam_->release();
 	if (ret) {
 		GST_ELEMENT_WARNING(self, RESOURCE, BUSY,
